          %p
            This makes it easy to understand the join as a kind of directed/lopsided
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B
            would be the colimit of the same diagram but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ←
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0] \rightarrow \{0,1\} \leftarrow [0]
            rather than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0] \rightarrow [1] \leftarrow [0]
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              If the small categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,C'
              are two posets, their join consists of their
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
            %li
              The monoidal structure induced on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Cat
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              is not symmetric (if it was, then the right cone of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              would be equivalent to the left cone, which is blatantly false);
            %li
              The monoidal structure induced on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Cat
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              is not closed, since the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\star -
              does not preserve colimits.
            %li
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cat
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\star C'\colon \Cat \to C'\!/\!\Cat\colon A\mapsto (A\to A\star C')
              is a left adjoint, and similarly is the functor
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\star-
              %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/crm/hocat/advanced-course/Quadern45-2.pdf#page=96"} Joyal, Ch. 3.1.1-2
              for a detailed description.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              The
              %strong cone
              below a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the join
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} pt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \star \mathrm{pt}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the join
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} pt
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{pt} \star C
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+topological+spaces"} join of topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+quasi-categories"}> join of quasi-categories
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+simplicial+sets"}> join of simplicial sets
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
          %h2#references References
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0608/0608040v4.pdf#page=42"} p. 42
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em Higher topos theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0608040"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            See also
            %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/crm/hocat/advanced-course/Quadern45-2.pdf#page=95"} Ch. 3
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em The theory of quasicategories and its applications
              lectures at
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://mat.uab.cat/~kock/crm/hocat/advanced-course/Quadern45-2.pdf"} pdf
